WEBVTT

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.270
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.270
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:13.570
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:13.570
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:18.950
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:18.950
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:24.240
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:24.240
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.580
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.580
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.840
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.840
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.220
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.220
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:46.310
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:46.310
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:51.860
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:51.860
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.940
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.940
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.240
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.240
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:07.500
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:07.500
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.170
namida kareru made

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.170
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.220
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.220
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.550
namida hareru made

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.550
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:28.560
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:28.560
though I may lose my way,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.400
egakikake no ima

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.400
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.900
kizamu

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:39.650
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.190
akashi

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:39.650
kono te de

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.350
Damn!

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.220
Out!

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.790
Game over!

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.400
No one can stop the Hornets' momentum!

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:14.230
The Coyotes lost today, putting the Hornets only two games behind.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:20.230
That last one was a bad pitch, but you got lucky with the batter.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.330
It wasn't like you.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.660
Yeah, it just slipped out of my hand.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.790
I'll be more careful next time.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.480
How did you pull off three hits and a home run?

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.710
Yeah, no kidding.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.130
Well, I was just in the zone today.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.050
We can't be losing when those guys won their division title.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.660
Which guys?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.990
Yeah, who do you mean?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:48.890
That's Not Like You!

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:48.890
That's Not Like You!

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.520
Go! Go! Bats!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.790
Safe! Safe!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.960
All right!

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.840
Kelloge's doing great.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.670
Yeah.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:28.680
He'll definitely get called up to the majors this year.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.240
All right, Shigeno.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.960
Let's call it a day.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.910
Yeah.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.770
Is he still practicing?

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.100
He's working way too hard.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.970
What's up, guys?

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.540
Check it out.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.680
Roy's gotten himself way too excited.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.680
He's a completely different person just because it's September 1st tomorrow.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.560
September 1st?

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.720
Don't you remember?

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.020
They're expanding the roster tomorrow.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.350
Oh, yeah!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:19.440
I'm sure he's nervous that he might lose some attention.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.640
I don't know what he's thinking.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.420
I see nothing wrong with that.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.370
I hear we'll be getting some great players this year.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.800
If you just stand around, you might lose your spot in the starting lineup.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.560
W-We can't let that happen!

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.460
Yeah, that'd be bad.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.560
Hey, Roy!

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.630
Let me go!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:39.910
No, I'm first!

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.380
Get real. I am!

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.480
Expanding the roster, huh?

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:48.630
I remember I couldn't sleep the night before, when I was in the minors.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:52.430
I kept thinking, "I might become a major leaguer tomorrow."

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.290
And you were sleeping out of frustration the next day, right?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.730
Shut up!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:02.950
I heard Quezada will be coming up to pitch and Kelloge and Battler will be fielders.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:05.540
Kelloge, especially, is doing great this year.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.800
Oh, I see.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.240
No wonder Roy's training so hard.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.950
Roy and Kelloge started the same year.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.830
They're both close friends and rivals.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.450
They swore that they'd be in the majors together.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.000
Really?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.260
You're right, they were pretty close.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.470
Well, my turn.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.930
I'm beat.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:28.930
Damn.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.860
Hey, get this!

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.140
I got a call from Kelloge yesterday.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.830
He was like, "I'll turn the Hornets into champions!"

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.560
Man, he hasn't even been called up yet.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.350
He thinks he's being funny.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:50.570
I got a call from the top earlier.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.740
Congratulations!

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.000
You're all major leaguers starting tomorrow.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.420
All right!

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:58.420
Yes!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.470
We did it!

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.850
We finally did it!

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:01.830
Yeah!

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:06.550
Hey, you guys going up to the majors?

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.260
Yeah.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.000
We'll have to leave the play-offs in your hands.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.720
Better bring us back another trophy this year.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.780
You bet!

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.980
And I better not see your faces here again.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:15.890
You won't!

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.560
Kelloge!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.030
I just got a call from your house.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.520
It's urgent, your father's...

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.900
Hey, we're here.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.200
Battler! Quezada!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.900
It's been a while.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:35.870
We've been waiting.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:37.460
Hey, General!

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.100
Looks like you've gotten pretty comfortable as stadium personnel.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:40.910
Huh?

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:41.800
Well, look at you!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.430
You seem to be busy going up and down every year.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.760
Wh-What?!

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.230
You're not even a player!

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:49.300
Say that again?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.010
You've been playing really well lately.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.390
I was pretty worried when you came back with the yips.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.560
Yeah, I've managed.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.530
Hey, Keene!

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:03.560
We'll be playing again starting today.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.250
He's as antisocial as ever...

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.240
Hey, what happened to Kelloge?

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.700
He got called up, right?

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.400
Well...

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:19.910
His father collapsed, so he went home...

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.630
I hear he's going to retire from baseball.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.600
Wh-What the hell?!

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:38.410
Battler, it's your first time in the majors, right?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.800
Are you nervous?

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.310
A-Are you kidding me?

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.230
I'll show everyone how I turned the Bats into champions.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:54.830
Roy.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.230
I was calling Kelloge to ask him what happened myself,

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.280
but he's not answering.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:02.550
He's probably busy.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.020
The game's starting, so let's head back.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:08.820
A-Aren't you worried?!

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.010
Oh, sorry.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.260
It's just... when I think about his feelings...

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.670
Hey, Shigeno.

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:23.800
You stayed on with the Bats last year when you were called up, right?

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:24.440
Yeah.

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.610
I was pretty hesitant to come up too.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.240
I mean, I was happy,

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.280
but when I thought about the Bats being in the play-offs,

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:36.190
I wondered if I could really just come to the majors.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:38.200
But when I told him that, he told me...

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.640
Are you stupid?!

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:42.570
You're gonna blow off a chance at the majors?!

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.290
Hurry up and get out of here!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.960
You're hardly useful around here!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.590
We'll win the play-offs on our own.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.010
He's been completely obsessed with making it to the majors ever since he was a rookie.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:09:00.930
When his chance finally came, his father collapsed.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:07.550
Honestly, I don't mind playing for the Bats forever.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:08.810
You idiot!

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.400
If you say that again, I'll kick you off the Bats!

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.620
An obsession with the majors, huh?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:24.970
Out!

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:29.020
I know the major and minor leagues are different,

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.000
but we're all baseball players.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.800
There can't be this much of a difference.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.390
Safe!

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:52.420
H-Hey...

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:55.030
Were the Hornets... this strong?

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.280
Strike out!

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.210
Swing out!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.920
This is the team that hasn't won a title in twenty-five years?

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:15.840
Seriously.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:19.440
I heard the Hornets are different this year.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:22.140
Looks like we really need to step up our game,

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.060
or we'll never get to bat.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.150
What is he doing?!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.570
Hey, idiot!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.160
Where do you think you're throwing?

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:46.370
O-Oh, sorry.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:51.150
Roy's still a moody guy, just like he was in the minors.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.260
Yeah.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.500
Don't worry, Roy!

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.890
It's just an error.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.840
Three straight wins since the game with the Grippers.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.480
Hey, how did the Coyotes do?

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.840
They won.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.560
We're still two games behind.

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.110
Man, they're strong too.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.750
Nice pitching today, Shigeno.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.710
What's so nice about getting switched out at the end?

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:32.540
You didn't get switched out because they didn't have confidence in you.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:35.370
They just don't want you to be tired for the next game.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.630
Tired?!

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.690
My shoulder doesn't even warm up until after 100 pitches!

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.250
Shigeno, Sanders,

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.220
Roy, and Dunstan.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.850
Are you guys free after this?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.380
Y-Yeah.

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:48.490
Why?

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:52.640
Oh, we're throwing a farewell party for Kelloge with the guys from the Bats.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:55.470
We're going to Memphis right now, so want to come?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.570
Oh, for Kelloge?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.060
Sure, I'll go.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.970
Me too.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.560
W-Wait a minute!

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.170
Kelloge's retiring when he just got promoted to the majors!

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:08.800
If we all go there as major leaguers, then...

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:10.310
What are you saying?

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.110
Kelloge's the one who invited you.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:15.710
He wanted to see the guys from the Hornets too, so he told us to grab you.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.130
Kelloge did?

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.420
Keene, you're coming too, right?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.630
No, thanks.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.110
What, you already have other plans?

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.810
I don't socialize.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:29.560
If I were Kelloge, I wouldn't want to see anyone who made it.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.030
And if he feels different,

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:33.920
I guess he doesn't even have his pride.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.520
H-Hey!

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.630
Damn, what's his problem?

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:41.200
Don't mind him.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.150
You're coming, right, Roy?

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.650
Y-Yeah.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:48.100
What about you, Shigeno?

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.990
Yeah, I'll go.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:54.710
I'd like to see the other guys from the Bats.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:07.880
I get that Kelloge's retiring, but what's he gonna do from now on?

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:11.910
His dad runs a big toy store in Louisiana.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:15.080
I'm sure he'll help with the business while he takes care of his dad.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.900
A toy store, huh?

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.780
So he's gonna be the manager of a toy store.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:21.820
He said that the local kids love it.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.810
Hey, you're here!

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.420
It's been a while, guys.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.020
Boss!

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.480
Miss Alice.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.590
It's been a while.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:45.830
Come on in.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:47.570
They're all inside.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:51.620
Shigeno, I'm glad you got over your yips.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:52.470
Yeah...

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.850
Want some?

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.920
Potato chips!

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:57.020
Kidding.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.390
He's already drunk...

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.910
Hey, I see some nostalgic faces.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.410
Welcome to Memphis.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.320
Guys, have a blast tonight!

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:29.880
Some people come all the way from Texas to shop at our store.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:33.910
Once the business picks up some more, I'm gonna open up a few more branches and maybe start franchising.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.100
Just watch,

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:39.040
I'll attract kids from all over the states.

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:41.310
Doesn't that sound great, Shigeno?

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.330
Yeah, it sure does.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.850
I didn't know you liked kids that much.

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:49.200
Gonna bid farewell to sweaty baseball.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:52.770
I'll earn ten times as much as rookie major leaguers.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:58.040
Hey, man, what's up, Roy?

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.660
You're looking awfully down, man.

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:01.410
What?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.710
Th-That's not true.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.230
Do you know about this?

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.980
It's the Ribbit Monster!

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:10.380
This is like the big thing with the kids right now.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.250
Hey, sonny Roy!

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:13.820
How are you doing, ribbit?

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.810
I'll tickle you, ribbit!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:17.810
Hey, stop.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.980
With a face like that, you're gonna get constipated, ribbit.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:24.940
Stop!

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:33.870
This is fine?

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:39.520
Are you seriously fine quitting baseball?!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.390
What?

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.670
I told you that I'm gonna be the Toy King of America.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:46.590
I don't have time to play baseball.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:50.010
We made a promise to play in the majors together!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:50.740
Yet...

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.760
How can you act so happy right now?

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.210
Did...

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:57.180
Did baseball ever mean anything to you?

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.890
Mean something to me?

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:04.110
Don't be ridiculous!

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:06.110
Are you twelve, or what?

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.310
Are you saying

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.700
that I could continue baseball with just meaning alone?

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:19.540
My dad's in the hospital and I can't let my mom take all the burden.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.830
I must support them.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.460
Am I fine quitting baseball?

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.130
Of course not!

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.230
I got called up!

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.430
I was able to become a major leaguer!

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:36.220
My life-long dream finally came true.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:38.490
But...

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.640
That doesn't mean I can do anything.

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:54.370
I see.

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:59.240
You were just forcing yourself to be overzealous.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:04.170
No wonder you looked like a kid forcing a smile after losing a fight.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.330
What?!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.150
H-Hey.

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:09.560
Shigeno.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:14.090
Even if you did get to the majors,
a coward like you wouldn't be useful.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.680
Thanks for doing us a favor and retiring.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.370
Shigeno, what are you saying?

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:20.760
Now you've done it.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.430
We're taking this outside!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.060
Let's have a match, Shigeno!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:27.600
See if I have a shot in the majors!

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.570
I'll take the offer.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:33.030
They didn't let me throw enough today, so this is perfect.

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.090
It's a one out game.

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:47.790
Got it?

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.060
Yeah.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.630
Better get serious, Kelloge.

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:57.050
He's not the Shigeno you knew on the Bats.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.680
Yeah, I know.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.170
That's a strike.

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:16.320
It's even faster than it was last year.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:20.570
So that's the pitch that strikes major leaguers out.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.050
Wh—

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:31.840
A forkball?

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.210
At that speed?

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:35.890
Strike two!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.800
Man, Shigeno...

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.050
He didn't have to use a forkball there.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.240
This is a serious match.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:50.480
Shigeno acknowledges him as an elite batter.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.720
Kelloge, loosen up your shoulders!

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:55.850
What happened to your usual batting?

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.550
That's right.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.570
I can't just lose without a fight.

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.530
I got called up.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.490
So, at least for today,

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.680
I'm a...

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.870
major leaguer!

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:29.470
A fly to the pitcher...

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.370
Damn it!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.380
Kelloge.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.040
That was a nice swing.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:56.460
As good as a cleanup in the majors.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.320
Shigeno.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:19:59.880
This isn't like you, Kelloge.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.750
You've got a strong desire to play baseball.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:06.630
Fight until the very last moment.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:12.600
What happened to the Kelloge who yelled at me to strive for the majors?

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.650
This isn't like me, huh?

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:23.140
Damn, I was going to hit a home run and retire on a high note.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.930
But it looks like I have homework now.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:29.510
I don't know how long it'll be,

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:31.120
but let's have another match, Shigeno.

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:35.670
When I come back to the majors.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.130
Kelloge.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.450
You bet.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.310
Roy.

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:47.850
You better not get demoted until I come back to the majors.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:49.760
Yeah!

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:52.540
And you better come back!

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.240
And the runner scores!

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:13.480
Watts let in a run!

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.350
He failed to defend and now it's all tied up!

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.740
The White Hawks have tied the game in the ninth.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:27.510
This is a great chance for the Hornets to end the game.

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:31.620
They've put a runner on second with a sacrifice bunt and two outs.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.510
And we're back to the top of the lineup.

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:37.690
Play!

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:40.730
Strike!

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.110
Who would've thought Watts would give up a run.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:44.530
Two outs and a runner on second.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.700
If we don't get a run, we're going into extra innings.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:52.830
Fight until the very last moment.

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.190
Safe! Safe!

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:08.450
What a comeback!

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:10.540
The closer gave up a run,

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:12.470
but Roy turned it around with his RBI!

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:14.730
That's the fourth consecutive win for the Hornets!

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:19.820
The Coyotes lost today, so the Hornets are only one game off the lead!

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:22.020
Hey, Junior.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:23.030
Let's go.

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:23.730
Yeah.

00:22:28.970 --> 00:22:31.030
You're here, Hornets.

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:34.210
The division's finally starting to get interesting.

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:51.960
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:51.960
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:58.680
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:58.680
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:00.350
yume wo

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:03.520
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:01.220 --> 00:23:03.520
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:06.310
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:09.520
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:09.520
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:13.490
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:13.490
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:14.150 --> 00:23:20.910
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:14.150 --> 00:23:20.910
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.530 --> 00:23:28.210
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.530 --> 00:23:28.210
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:32.960
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:35.980
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:35.980
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:38.590
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:43.640
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.590 --> 00:23:40.350
kizukazu ni

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:43.640
suki ni natta

00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:45.930
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:50.770
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:50.770
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:53.360
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:58.450
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:55.240
otagai ni

00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:58.450
hikareteita

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:00.660
kono kimochi wa

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:07.660
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:07.660
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:15.780
Preview

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:15.780
Preview

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:12.300
All right!

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:14.620
We're only one game from the top.

00:24:14.620 --> 00:24:19.970
With my pitching, I'll catch the Coyotes' tails in the next big game.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:21.850
That's what I'd like to say, but...

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:25.440
Next time, on Major: The Creeping Shadow.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:27.680
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:31.120
Next Time

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:31.120
Next Time

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:31.120
The Creeping Shadow

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:31.120
The Creeping Shadow
